"""Net part 2: the replicated values (net/net_track.cpp lines 20-end: the track, the position track, the direction
track) against the original's (net/track_diff.cpp, suite net.track; run with HD2_TRACK_QUICK=1 on build_track.bat,
linked with -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000).

472 mutants, 46 not building; 374 of the 426 building killed. The first run left 72: exact edges (squares at 1e-16, a
distance at the snap distance, a turn of exactly 0.001, EndRead's square at 1e-16, a derived rate near 0.1, distances
of exactly 0.785 and half the angles' span), the direction track's short way round taken and moving, the rate's w after
a base Read (the test had left that word out on every track; only the direction track's EndRead leaves it undefined)
were not in the cases; they are now. The 52 left:
- Unreachable: EndRead's tiny-rate branch (350-355, 15 mutants): the speed is over 8 there, so the square is over 64.
- Equivalent: Magnitude's and EndRead's |square - 1| < 1e-8 (28, 344 cmp, num, arith): a float square is either 1
  (whose root is 1) or at least 6e-8 from it; EndRead's square >= 1e-8 (345 cmp): over 64; the empty BeginWrite and
  BeginRead (159, 209 del); arrays one larger (165, 217 num); Write's deltas worked out again (177-179, 182-184 del,
  num: the same values are in place; 179 / 184 num write the slot past the array); the angle quantisations made again
  (272 del, bool: the same); the span's terms swapped (322, 379 num, code: the angle quantisation's three ranges are
  equal); the speed's sign (341 cmp, num: always over 8); a speed of exactly 8 scaled to 8 (339 cmp: the same rate);
  the read and derived rates at 1e-16 (232, 240 cmp: quantised values are 0 or a step's square apart).
- Narrow: Magnitude's floor exactly (26 cmp: no float squares to 0x322bcc77); the derived and read rates' squares at
  exactly 0.1 and 0.02 (230, 238 cmp: squares of quantised values)."""
